# What `railway up` must NOT upload. Used with `railway up --no-gitignore`, which
# stops the CLI from applying .gitignore so gitignored custom template kits
# (inertia/custom/kits/*) are uploaded and compiled into the image. Everything
# else .gitignore excludes is re-excluded here. Keep the two in sync: anything
# added to .gitignore that must not reach Railway needs a line here too.
# See docs/RAILWAY_DEPLOYMENT.md → "Deploying without GitHub".

# VCS / tooling
.git
.claude
.fleet
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# Dependencies + build output (Railway installs and builds from scratch)
node_modules
build
public/assets
.vite

# Secrets — never ship local env files; Railway injects its own variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Self-hosted release layout + local runtime data. `public/uploads` is a
# symlink to `shared/uploads` created by scripts/build-release.mjs for VPS-style
# deploys — Railway needs neither, and if `shared/uploads` doesn't exist locally
# (a fresh clone that never ran a self-hosted release) the CLI's upload fails
# trying to read the broken symlink. Excluded outright.
releases/
shared/
current
current.next
public/uploads
# Leading slash: root-level runtime storage only. A bare `storage/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth (same class of bug the repo's own
# .gitignore warns about for modules/* and inertia/custom/kits/*) — it was
# silently swallowing app/services/storage/ (real source, incl. driver.ts),
# so `railway up` never uploaded it at all. Every "Cannot find module
# .../storage/driver.*" failure on Railway was this, not a Node loader bug.
/storage/
tmp/*
!tmp/.gitkeep

# Codegen regenerated during the build (the Tuyau registry is the exception —
# the build needs it and never regenerates it)
/.adonisjs/*
!/.adonisjs/client/
/.adonisjs/client/*
!/.adonisjs/client/registry/
app/services/*.generated.ts
inertia/css/*.generated.css
database/schema.ts
